 Expected actual comparison: control -1/EPERM versus candidate0/errno0 supports the cause hypothesis. EPERM in both falsifies the seccomp-only remedy. Unexpected control success or other errno requires diagnosis. No outcome resets the stopped browser-canary counter or accepts Playwright. Parent/child namespace behavior, procfs permissions, actual Perl startup/ELF behavior, return/errno, container inspect/cleanup and final browser compatibility are all unexecuted. The prepared command manifest is not execution authorization.
+
+## Preparation fix1 — runtime identity lifecycle only
+
+Independent review found the anonymous `run --rm` prerequisite could leave an unidentifiable worker after interruption. `commands.json.runtime_identity_preflight` now specifies exact-name pre-absence/create/inspect/start-attach/post-inspect/finally force-remove/post-absence. The fixed name is `altera-chroot-identity-97bd451e7177`; all actual output/command/exit records have private, bounded targets under `evidence/runtime-identity/`. A 15-second outer watchdog, exact created-ID/config verification before start, strict bounded result validation, and unconditional targeted finally cleanup after create success are mandatory. Final absence must be positively verified even after failure. An existing name refuses creation and is never cleaned by this operation.
+
+The original Node built-ins-only readback expression and all image/platform/security/resources inputs are byte-for-byte retained; only lifecycle identity changes. Built-in seccomp, no mounts/network, UID/GID1000, cap-dropALL, no-new-privileges and read-only root remain fixed. The two arms, both profile JSON files and Perl probe are unchanged. `fix1/*.before` preserves original manifest/report/hash snapshot; `fix1/fix-only.diff` and `fix1/static-proof.json` record the correction. Static assertions verified sole manifest section change, exact preserved Node/security argv tail, output coverage and absence of mount/profile override. No Docker or helper rerun occurred; runtime presence/identity and Linux behavior remain unknown. This JSON requires an enforcing trusted coordinator; it is not an executor or authorization. Browser failure count remains 2.
